<title>USA: U.S. crop progress highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. crop progress highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Monday said six percent of the U.S. winter wheat crop was in very poor condition, 13 percent in poor, 35 percent fair, 40 percent good and six percent excellent.</p>
<p>The report reflected the impact of a cold snap that damaged winter wheat crops in Kansas, Oklahoma and Texas.</p>
<p>In its report on April 20 conditions, USDA said 60 percent of the Kansas wheat crop rated very poor to fair versus only 37 percent last week. In Oklahoma, 58 percent of the crop was in very poor to fair condition versus 34 percent last week. And in Texas, 68 percent of the wheat rated very poor to fair versus 39 percent last week.</p>
</text>
